## Source

rf2-i3ffz audit, finding F-CORR-3.

## What

`test/_runner.js:75-99` performs cleanup inside the `try` body:

```js
try {
  await client.connect(transport);
  await body(client, transport);
  await client.close();        // <-- can throw
  clearTimeout(watchdog);
  process.exit(0);
} catch (err) {
  try { await client.close(); } catch (_e) {}
  clearTimeout(watchdog);
  process.exit(1);
}
```

If `body` returns successfully but the success-path `client.close()` throws, the catch block fires AGAIN with a different error, and the success state of `body` is lost in the log. `clearTimeout(watchdog)` belongs in a `finally`.

## Fix

Refactor to:

```js
try {
  await client.connect(transport);
  await body(client, transport);
  exitCode = 0;
} catch (err) {
  ... log err ...
  exitCode = 1;
} finally {
  try { await client.close(); } catch {}
  clearTimeout(watchdog);
  process.exit(exitCode);
}
```

## LoC

~10 LoC delta.

## Severity

P2 — eliminates a class of "silent log inversion" bugs ahead of causa-mcp impl landing.

Audit rf2-wnvcd MF-3: rf2-69ad2 registered :rf.ssr/check-version and :rf.ssr/check-schema-digest fxs in implementation/ssr/src/re_frame/ssr.cljc. The fxs emit three new trace ops: :rf.ssr/version-mismatch, :rf.ssr/schema-digest-mismatch, :rf.ssr/compatibility-check-skipped. Spec 011-SSR.md §The :rf/hydrate event describes them in prose.

Drift: spec/009-Instrumentation.md §Error event catalogue is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for every :rf.ssr/* category (per Ownership.md line 39 — 'The §Error event catalogue is the single source of truth for every :rf.error/*, :rf.warning/*, :rf.fx/*, :rf.cofx/*, :rf.ssr/*, :rf.epoch/*, :rf.http/*, :rf.frame/*, :route.nav-token/* category — id · :op-type · trigger · default :recovery · :tags (per rf2-wfbn3)'). The catalogue currently lists only :rf.ssr/hydration-mismatch. The three new :rf.ssr/* ops are emitted by impl and prose-described in 011, but missing from the closed catalogue.

Fix: Add three rows to the 009 §Error event catalogue:
- :rf.ssr/version-mismatch — :warning, trigger 'payload :rf/version differs from runtime', default :recovery :warned-and-replaced, :tags {:frame :expected :actual}
- :rf.ssr/schema-digest-mismatch — :warning, trigger 'payload schema-digest differs from runtime', default :recovery :warned-and-replaced, :tags {:frame :expected :actual}
- :rf.ssr/compatibility-check-skipped — :warning, trigger 'check fx fired but no actual-value hook registered', default :recovery :logged-and-skipped, :tags {:check :reason}

